@startuml SQLGenie_MCP_DataFlow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam roundcorner 15

title SQLGenie MCP - Data Flow Architecture

!define LIGHTBLUE #E8F4FD
!define LIGHTGREEN #E8F8E8
!define LIGHTYELLOW #FFF8DC
!define LIGHTPINK #FFE8E8
!define LIGHTGRAY #F5F5F5

' External Entities
rectangle "User" as user LIGHTBLUE
rectangle "Claude Desktop" as claude LIGHTBLUE
rectangle "VS Code Terminal" as terminal LIGHTYELLOW

' Processes
circle "1.0\nNatural Language\nProcessing" as nlp LIGHTGREEN
circle "2.0\nMCP Protocol\nHandling" as mcp LIGHTGREEN
circle "3.0\nTool\nDispatch" as dispatch LIGHTGREEN
circle "4.0\nSecurity\nValidation" as security LIGHTPINK
circle "5.0\nDatabase\nQuery" as dbquery LIGHTGREEN
circle "6.0\nResult\nAnalysis" as analysis LIGHTGREEN
circle "7.0\nResponse\nFormatting" as format LIGHTGREEN

' Data Stores
cylinder "D1\nSakila\nDatabase" as sakila_db LIGHTGRAY
cylinder "D2\nUploaded\nDatabases" as user_db LIGHTGRAY
cylinder "D3\nSchema\nCache" as cache LIGHTGRAY
rectangle "D4\nConfiguration\nFiles" as config LIGHTGRAY

' Data Flows
user --> nlp : **DF1: Natural Language Query**\n"Show me customers from California"

nlp --> claude : **DF2: Intent Recognition**\n{intent: "database_query",\ntarget: "customer_data",\nfilter: "California"}

claude --> mcp : **DF3: MCP Tool Request**\n{"method": "tools/call",\n"name": "execute_sql_query",\n"args": {...}}

mcp --> dispatch : **DF4: Parsed Tool Call**\n{tool: "execute_sql_query",\ndatabase_id: "sakila",\nquery: "SELECT ..."}

dispatch --> security : **DF5: Raw Parameters**\n{database_id, query, options}

security --> security : **DF6: Validation Results**\n{is_safe: true,\nsanitized_query: "...",\nlimits_applied: {...}}

alt Query Validation Success
    security --> dbquery : **DF7: Validated Request**\n{safe_query, connection_params}
    
    dbquery --> cache : **DF8: Schema Lookup**\n{database_id, table_names}
    cache --> dbquery : **DF9: Cached Schema**\n{tables: {...}, relationships: {...}}
    
    alt Schema Cache Miss
        dbquery --> sakila_db : **DF10a: Schema Query**\n"PRAGMA table_info(...)"
        sakila_db --> dbquery : **DF11a: Schema Data**\n{columns, types, constraints}
        dbquery --> cache : **DF12a: Cache Update**\n{schema_json, timestamp}
    else Schema Cache Hit
        note over cache : Use cached schema
    end
    
    dbquery --> sakila_db : **DF13: Data Query**\n"SELECT c.first_name, c.last_name..."
    sakila_db --> dbquery : **DF14: Raw Results**\n{rows: [...], metadata: {...}}
    
    dbquery --> user_db : **DF15: Alternative Query**\n(if different database selected)
    user_db --> dbquery : **DF16: Alternative Results**
    
    dbquery --> analysis : **DF17: Query Results**\n{data: [...], query_info: {...}}
    
    analysis --> analysis : **DF18: Pattern Analysis**\n{insights: [...], statistics: {...}}
    
    analysis --> format : **DF19: Analyzed Results**\n{results: [...], insights: [...], summary: "..."}
    
else Query Validation Failure
    security --> format : **DF20: Security Error**\n{error: "Dangerous operation",\nallowed_operations: [...]}
end

format --> mcp : **DF21: Formatted Response**\n{"success": true, "results": [...],\n"explanation": "Found 45 customers..."}

mcp --> claude : **DF22: MCP Response**\n{tool_result: {...}, status: "success"}

claude --> nlp : **DF23: AI Processing**\n{structured_data: [...], context: {...}}

nlp --> user : **DF24: Natural Language Response**\n"I found 45 customers from California.\nHere are the results: [table]\nInsights: Most are from Los Angeles..."

' Configuration flows
config --> mcp : **DF25: Server Config**\n{connection_settings, tool_definitions}
config --> security : **DF26: Security Rules**\n{allowed_operations, limits, timeouts}

' Terminal monitoring
terminal --> mcp : **DF27: Process Control**\n{start, stop, restart}
mcp --> terminal : **DF28: Status Updates**\n{running, errors, logs}

' Error handling flows
security --> format : **DF29: Validation Errors**\n{sql_errors, security_violations}
dbquery --> format : **DF30: Database Errors**\n{connection_errors, query_failures}
analysis --> format : **DF31: Analysis Warnings**\n{large_result_sets, performance_hints}

' Performance monitoring
dbquery --> cache : **DF32: Performance Metrics**\n{query_time, result_size, cache_hits}
cache --> analysis : **DF33: Usage Statistics**\n{access_patterns, performance_data}

' Legend for data flow types
note bottom
**Data Flow Legend:**
• **DF1-4:** User Interface Layer
• **DF5-7:** Security & Validation
• **DF8-16:** Database Operations
• **DF17-19:** Analysis & Processing
• **DF20-24:** Response Generation
• **DF25-28:** Configuration & Control
• **DF29-33:** Error Handling & Monitoring
end note

' Data store descriptions
note right of sakila_db
**Sakila Database:**
• 16 tables
• Movie rental domain
• Sample data included
• Read-only access
end note

note right of user_db
**User Databases:**
• Uploaded .db files
• Custom schemas
• Business data
• Cached metadata
end note

note right of cache
**Schema Cache:**
• JSON metadata
• Table structures
• Relationships
• Performance data
end note

note right of config
**Configuration:**
• claude_desktop_config.json
• Security policies
• Connection settings
• Tool definitions
end note

@enduml